Volume = {27},
Number = {12},
Pages = {1182-1187},
Abstract = {The configuration and operation of the navigational locks in Seattle,
   Washington, USA is such that large numbers of boats are congregated in a
   small confined area, implying a potential health risk to boat operators
   and passengers from engine exhaust. Air samples (141) were taken from a
   boat during peak traffic periods and analyzed for CO, NO2 and aldehydes.
   Weather and traffic data were also recorded. Of the CO samples, 6\% were
   of sufficient concentration and duration to possibly cause adverse
   cardiovascular effects and change time perception. Concentrations of
   aldehydes and NO2 often exceed their respective odor and irritation
   thresholds. The highest pollutant concentrations generally occurred when
   the traffic was traveling east in the large lock, the number of boats
   was over 50 and the lockage duration was over 20 min.},
